            <ArticleTitle>Local anesthesia: an appropriate technology for simple fistula repair.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S75-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To assess the efficacy of local infiltrative anesthesia with lidocaine hydrochloride in patients undergoing the surgical repair of a simple vesico-vaginal fistula.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The study was carried out with 21 patients undergoing the repair of a simple midvaginal vesico-vaginal fistula. The patients' perception of pain was evaluated intraoperatively.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Most patients indicated that the anesthetic agent provided adequate analgesia, and all fistulas were repaired successfully without postoperative complications.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Repairing simple vesico-vaginal fistulas is feasible with a local infiltrative anesthetic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
